    "created_at": "2025-02-20T06:15:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-02-20T06:15:00Z",
    "body": "> So I would argue that a rejected `play()` promise shouldn't show up via the \"unhandledrejection\" event.\n\nBut, the `play()` promise is not an \"user interaction event\", I don't see how this could apply here. \n\nFrom what I understand, the intent here was that one could handle all the [media events](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLMediaElement#events) on the element even when it's controlled by the native controls, but not the UI events themselves. So, e.g. you'd get the `playing`, `pause`, `seeked`, etc. events, but you wouldn't get the `pointermove` or `pointerup` ones that ended up triggering the method.  \n\nNow, the `play()` promise is also part of the \"media occurrences\" (to not say \"event\"), so it makes sense that it's there. However this whole *native controls fire media events* strategy was built before there was Promises in the mix, and these don't work with this model. So I believe they need to be called out explicitly.  \n\n(Might be noted that in the exposed case, the `abort` event will fire, so this *occurrence* can be handled from there.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
